The IR[ATA] Level 2 Rope Access course offers a wider range of knowledge and skills including, rigging working ropes, undertaking a wider range of rescues and performing rope access tasks. To progress to IR[ATA] Level 2 candidates must have at least 12 months and 1,000 working hours experience as an IR[ATA] Level 1 Technician. Candidates must also have knowledge of legislation and safety requirements relating to rope access such as the IRATA general requirements.
