NORMAN-05/DPC Add[endum] 4-A specifies that the structural features must be able to protect passengers from lateral, vertical and head impacts and must be made of[ stainless] steel bars of tubes and enable buoyant material to be attached around it, so that an entire fully loaded basket assembly is able to float.
In order to meet the Brazilian legislation, Reflex Marine has launched the[ FROG]-6, an operational tool that is able to provide a safe option for personnel transfers. The FR[OG]-6 has been subjected to a variety of impact tests to verify its structural integrity and shock-absorbing capability and demonstrated its ability to self-align and float in water, something that is not possible with the traditional rope baskets.
